# Without this, every checkout on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF and git reports "LF will be
# replaced by CRLF" on each commit touching src/ or dist/. Line endings also change file
# hashes, which silently breaks any digest pinned over a tracked text file.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the directories this repo authors. A blanket `*` rule would also
# rewrite the 331 vendored node_modules files and the _decoded/ + .mhtml captures -- and the
# captures are evidence, which must keep matching what the browser saved byte for byte.
src/** text=auto eol=lf
tests/** text=auto eol=lf
tools/** text=auto eol=lf
dist/** text=auto eol=lf
docs/** text=auto eol=lf
*.md text=auto eol=lf
*.json text=auto eol=lf
*.gitignore text=auto eol=lf
*.gitattributes text=auto eol=lf

*.zip binary
*.png binary
